    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2760",
      "problem": "What is the surface area of the triangular prism represented by the net below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249141/assets/dafb07440f60418465b579aad73119cd47d6def34ed0cf1229afc9affbb177e4.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 12+3\\times 48 \\\\  & =24+144 \\\\  & =168\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
